            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"part-8-functions-45-min\">Part 8 \u2014 Functions (45 min)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A function packages up a block of code so you can reuse it with\ndifferent inputs, instead of copy-pasting.</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">function_name</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">parameter</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">type</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"n\">return_type</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"Docstring: what the function does.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"o\">...</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">result</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Parameters</strong> are the inputs the function needs</li>\n<li>The <strong>return type hint</strong> (<code>-&gt; float</code>) documents what comes back</li>\n<li>The <strong>docstring</strong> (triple-quoted string right under <code>def</code>) is the\n  function's built-in documentation</li>\n</ul></span>"
